## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests · 8 Critical findings · 1 Medium**

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** suite. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called (achieving high line coverage), but almost nothing meaningful is verified. Bugs in price calculation, CSV formatting, search logic, etc. would all slip through.

---

### 🔴 Critical — False Confidence

#### 1. Coverage-Touching Pattern (systemic)

The entire class methodically calls every public method with no or trivial assertions. This inflates coverage to ~95% while verifying almost nothing.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
// no assertion

// FIX
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)

Never checks the price actually changed.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)

Never checks the product was actually removed.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

Doesn't even capture the return value in later use. Zero verification.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

#### 6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)

The most bug-prone method (arithmetic) has zero verification.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

#### 7. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)

Never checks that the product was actually imported.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
